ntsync-live: optimistic spin before a gated WAIT_ANY sleeps

A WAIT_ANY whose thread passes the gate (spin_ns set, realtime unless spin_rt=0, a spin_comm prefix) spins
TASK_RUNNING on q->signaled for up to spin_ns, clamped to the wait's own deadline, and stops early on
need_resched, a signal or another runnable task on the CPU. The stock sleep loop then runs unchanged, so a
wake-up cannot be lost. WAIT_ALL never spins.

